backup.text:
Settings from an older Spiderweb ({old}) were found. A backup of them was made before this version uses them, in case you want them back:

{folder}

Your settings, palettes, saved shapes and presets are in it. Your projects and autosave are not touched.

about.not_moved:
Spiderweb now keeps its own files (autosave, saved shapes, presets…) in the user folder, but these couldn't be moved there (another program may be using them):

{files}

They are still in:
{here}

Close Spiderweb and move them into:
{user}

Until then Spiderweb starts without them.

errors.spiderweb_couldn_t_start_because_:
Spiderweb couldn't start because of an error.

{where}

Please include spiderweb-error.log when you report it.

project.autosave_failed:
Spiderweb can't save your work on its own (the autosave):
{path}
{e}

Until that's fixed, use File → Save as… to keep your work in a project file somewhere else.

project.autosave_failed_closing:
Your work couldn't be saved on its own (the autosave):
{path}
{e}

Save it as a project file before closing?

Yes = save it, No = close without saving, Cancel = stay open.

project.output_folder_missing:
The MIDI output folder saved in it isn't on this PC:
{folder}

MIDI files now go to Spiderweb's own output folder instead:
{path}

load.exported_own:
Saved the loaded MIDI ({notes}) with your shapes:
{path}

The file's own tracks are copied exactly as they were loaded.

load.exported_own_extracted:
Saved the loaded MIDI ({notes}) with your shapes:
{path}

Everything else in the file's own tracks is copied exactly as it was loaded.

load.exported_tempo:
